From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:04:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/20] wrappedmemory: return NULL from wrap() for another
 allocator

gst_wrapped_memory_allocator_memory_new() returns NULL for an allocator
that is not a wrapped memory one, and wrap() then handed that NULL to
gst_wrapped_memory_allocator_memory_set_data(), which fails a
gst_memory_is_type() precondition on it. Return the NULL directly.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/sailfishos/gst-droid/pull/91]
---
 gst-libs/gst/droid/gstwrappedmemory.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gst-libs/gst/droid/gstwrappedmemory.c b/gst-libs/gst/droid/gstwrappedmemory.c
index ec37eeb..c31e471 100644
--- a/gst-libs/gst/droid/gstwrappedmemory.c
+++ b/gst-libs/gst/droid/gstwrappedmemory.c
@@ -120,6 +120,10 @@ gst_wrapped_memory_allocator_wrap (GstAllocator * allocator,
 {
   GstMemory *mem = gst_wrapped_memory_allocator_memory_new (allocator, size);
 
+  if (!mem) {
+    return NULL;
+  }
+
   gst_wrapped_memory_allocator_memory_set_data (mem, data, cb, user_data);
 
   return mem;
